Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix oversized navbar and correct services/divisions grouping

- Navbar logo/header was 184px tall (logo forced to 172px), dwarfing
  the page and pushing hero content far down. Reduced to a normal
  84px header with a properly sized logo, introduced a --nav-h
  variable so the hero offset, section scroll-margin, mobile menu
  position, and footer logo all stay in sync.
- Services section previously merged 6 distinct offerings into 3
  mismatched cards (GIS/surveying dumped into IT Infrastructure;
  Web Dev, QA, Digital Transformation and Marketing all crammed
  into one 'Digital Solutions' card), while dedicated icons for
  surveying, QA and marketing already existed in the repo unused.
  Split into 6 accurate divisions (Security, Networks, Survey, Web,
  QA, Marketing), each with its own icon and correct service list.
- Updated footer Solutions list to match the 6 divisions, keeping
  it consistent with the services section and the contact form's
  existing 6-option service dropdown.
---
 index.html | 87 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 styles.css | 15 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

